course: dictionary
lesson: 9152
title: Nosy words: snooper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snooper is a person who secretly looks into other people's private business, or looks around where they should not. Snoop means to look nosily, and -er means a person who does it, so a snooper is someone who snoops.
explain: «Snooping can hurt the snooper too: you may read something unkind about yourself.» The sentence tells you that snooping means looking where you should not. The words "hurt the snooper too" show that prying into other people's things can backfire on the person doing it.
explain: A snooper can also be an official inspector who checks up on people, and this meaning often sounds disapproving. The context tells you which meaning is meant: a nosy neighbour peering through windows is a snooper in the first sense, while an inspector checking records is one in the official sense.
fact: A snooper is a person who secretly looks into other people's private business.
fact: «Snooping» means looking where you should not, especially into someone's private things.
fact: Snooper can also mean an official inspector checking up on people, often said in a disapproving way.
fact: Online, snoopers are people or apps trying to see your private information, so keep them out by keeping your passwords secret.
exercise: Her brother secretly reads her diary every day. What is he? | A lighthouse keeper | A gardener | A referee | *A snooper
exercise: «Snooping can hurt the snooper too.» What does snooper mean here? | A person who grows vegetables | *A person who secretly looks into other people's private business | A person who fixes bikes | A person who sings loudly at parties
exercise: In online safety, which is a snooper? | A bright lamp in your bedroom | *An app or person trying to see your private information | A friendly teacher marking your spelling test | A library book about birds
test: A nosy neighbour peeks through the window to read the letters on the kitchen table. What is the neighbour? | *A snooper | A referee | A postman | A florist
test: An inspector arrives to check the school kitchen, looking closely for mistakes. Which word fits in the official sense? | A baker | A singer | *A snooper | A sailor
exam: Which phrase best describes someone who secretly reads other people's letters? | Cheerful chef | Quiet kitten | Bouncy ball | *Nosy snooper
